== local outside a function is an error:
shit: 1:1: warning: A local outside a function has no scope to bind.
     1 |  local x=5
       |  ^~~~~
note: Declare the variable plainly or move it into a function.
shit: 1:1: error: Builtin `local`: Unable to declare a local variable outside a function.
     1 |  local x=5
       |  ^~~~~~~~~
note: `local` only works inside a function body.
rc=1
== local -i evaluates an integer assignment:
shit: 1:27: warning: An unquoted variable can split into words and expand globs.
     1 |  f(){ local -i n=3+4; echo $n; }; f
       |                            ^~
note: Quote the expansion to keep one argument.
7
== local -a declares an indexed array:
xy
== local -A declares an associative array:
val
== a local shadows an outer value and restores it:
shit: 1:35: warning: An unquoted variable can split into words and expand globs.
     1 |  v=outer; f(){ local v=inner; echo $v; }; f; echo $v
       |                                    ^~
note: Quote the expansion to keep one argument.
shit: 1:50: warning: An unquoted variable can split into words and expand globs.
     1 |  v=outer; f(){ local v=inner; echo $v; }; f; echo $v
       |                                                   ^~
note: Quote the expansion to keep one argument.
inner
outer
== fresh name warns:
1
== top-level name is quiet:
0
== inherited PATH is quiet:
0
rc=1
